table-alignment (MDL003), Tables
On by default, severity warning. Fixable.
markdownlint does not have this rule.

Each cell of a table's delimiter row has at least 3 dashes.

Why: GFM accepts a single dash, but 3 dashes make the row under the header easy
to see in the source.

Tags: table

Options, under rules.table-alignment.options:
  min_dashes (integer, default 3)
    Fewest dashes allowed in a cell of a table's delimiter row.

Fix: The fix lengthens each short run of dashes to the minimum and keeps any
colons. gomdlint may report a finding without a fix when the fix would change a
line with one character in brackets, such as [x] or [1], or the lines around it
up to a blank line, because it could add or remove a task list checkbox.

This document breaks the rule:
  | # Rules
  |
  | | Name | ID |
  | | - | - |
  | | line-length | MD013 |

gomdlint reports:
  4:1 Table delimiter has fewer than 3 dashes

The fix changes it to:
  | # Rules
  |
  | | Name | ID |
  | | --- | --- |
  | | line-length | MD013 |

Configure:
  rules:
    table-alignment:
      options:
        min_dashes: 3

Under rules, table-alignment: false turns the rule off and
table-alignment: error reports its findings as errors. The flag
--disable table-alignment turns it off for one run.

Silence one line:
  <!-- markdownlint-disable-next-line table-alignment -->
